Not a particularly exciting ascension, but this is my first from
playing nethack on and off for thirteen years or so.  I had watched an
ascension run of Eidolos on SomethingAwful and noticed that he used
Elbereth waaaaay more often than I ever had.  I think I had harbored
an elitist attitude about using it - maybe trying for an Elbereth-less
conduct that didn't exist?  Anyhow, after watching him play I decided
that maybe I would try my hand at ascending an elvish wizard too.

Several dead elf wizards later, I was happy with the performance of
Elbereth - I was making it much further per character than I had done
before.  And then my last one started up with a scrollbook of
identify.  Perhaps this is what made the run unexciting, because I
think that made the run a lot easier than it would've been otherwise.
An early ID turned up a wand of wishing(0:3) ... well, ok!  I wished
for two blessed SoC, got one.  Wished for +2 SDSM, got +0.  Found
speed boots, got BoH from sokoban.  The altar in Minetown was co-
algined and I had a bag of tricks, so I kept sacrificing until I got
Magicbane.

And then I made my rookie mistake.  Right after I got Magicbane, I
figured it was time to make some holy water.  Turns out that when your
god gives you a gift, you're not supposed to pray?  So I made Anhur
angry.  I lost the 4 points of protection I had bought so far (turns
out it is easier to make money from shopkeepers when you can ID your
gems!).  I did not have any holy water.  And Anhur stayed angry at me
for the entire rest of the game because I found no other altars, and
the scrolls and wands of create monster I used never made a baddie big
enough to slake Anhur's anger.

I poked around for a while before I finally caught a unicorn and got a
horn.  With that, the BoH, and the luckstone from Mine's End I was
about ready to burn a wish on some holy water when I found a spoiler
explaining how the atheist conduct players make their holy water.
Bleargh!  I wished for a blessed magic marker so I could make the
requisite scrolls, then it was finally off to the races!  I did a
teeny-tiny bit of polypiling with my stuff in Sokoban because I hadn't
been finding many wands or rings, and got a ring of conflict out of
the bargain.  Also wished for, then wrote, some blessed scrolls of
genocide, wiped out h, L, and ;.  A later throne genocide went to the
energy vortices, as I didn't want to lose my rings.

I was naturally level 14 for the quest, popped off the Dark One
without any trouble.  I wrote a book of magic missile about 2 dungeon
levels before finding one in a barracks.  Blew my way through Fort
Ludios and went back to buy the protection I had lost earlier.  Also,
slightly shamefully, wished for the Master Key of Thievery to reduce
the amount of physical damage I was taking.  I had thought about doing
it earlier but resisted temptation.  Waiting until later made me pay,
as I wasted a throne wish on it when I felt it in my hands but it
slipped away.  Finally used a /WoW on it and got it.

My last "oh no!" moment came at the castle when I was playing the
drawbridge game with the guys inside.  At some point I went to  use
the ; command to go figure out what one of the guys was and started
spamming "l" to move the cursor over.  Except, uh, I hadn't hit the ;
key, and I walked right into the moat.  Thankfully, instead of YASD, I
got a lot of blank spellbooks and paper, some diluted potions, and a
number of rusty wands.  Phew!

After that, it was pretty smooth sailing.  I had an AC of -28 from my
gear, and about 160HP at level 22.  I used a magic mapping spellbook
to map Gehemmon and used a pick-axe/spellbook of dig to clear a path
from staircase to staircase.  Popped Rodney with a wand of death,
levelported into the Sanctum and got lucky to skip almost all the
baddies.  Levitated back out with a wished-for cursed potion of gain
level (asked for 2, got 1 ... I'd say I had bad luck with my wished,
except that I was running around with my /WoW(0:3) from the castle
because I had already wished for everything I wanted . . . ) and ran
the heck out of there.

One of my favorite lucky turns from this game of lucky turns was when
I missed Rodney with my last charge in my wand of death.  I zapped
finger of death at him with a 66% fail rate; not only did it work, but
it hit and killed him.  Hurrah!  The planes were pretty easy, even air
because of the master key.  Unfortunately my inexperience showed and I
forgot to take off my ring of conflict before heading up to the Astral
Plane.  Oh well, the angry angels didn't do much to hurt me anyway.  I
was pretty surprised to find that my spell of jump didn't work in the
Astral Plane, but I ran around as best I could.

I had to go to all three altars before finding mine.  I death-rayed
Famine and never saw him again; good thing too, because my 28 K-
rations and 43 C-rations from Ludios were sitting in my stash in
Sokoban still ... whoops!  Death-rayed Pestilence, and teleported
Death out of my way about three times.  Quaffed two potions of full
healing while there, had a third blown up by somebody's wand or breath
ray.  Then ...

